---- registration ----
stored: $argon2id$v=19$m=2048,t=1,p=1$MDEyMzQ1Njc4OWFiY2RlZg$jG8xmIAnX1toMcew4aL4a/Dd89M8uHr/GFAJ9gGksl0

everything needed to check a password is in that string, and none of
it is a secret — the salt and costs are public by design

---- logging in ----
correct password      true (want true)
wrong password        false (want false)
empty password        false (want false)
case matters          false (want false)

---- a tampered database row ----
costs lowered to m=8  false (want false)
truncated encoding    false (want false)
empty stored value    false (want false)
bcrypt hash pasted in false (want false)

lowering the costs does not help an attacker: the parameters are
inputs to the hash, so changing them changes what the hash must be

---- two users, one password ----
user A  3c179fdc1f33d524f3e6375f4d5bfb6e…
user B  002281fe497c8d38bbf1d8175d90c566…
identical passwords, unrelated hashes: true (want true)

without per-user salts these two rows would be identical, and one
cracked password would unlock every account that shared it

---- upgrading the cost later ----
old hash            $argon2id$v=19$m=512,t=1,p=1$MDEyMzQ1Njc4OWFiY2RlZg$4wY/aKGqo2BgjzublOGUxmrZ/OsLDSn/Zd/5vUB4JqE
still verifies      true (want true)
flagged for rehash  true (want true)
current is fine     false (want false)

on a successful login you hold the plaintext for the only moment you
ever will — re-hash there, or the upgrade never reaches existing users

---- do not do this ----
sha256 unsalted     c4bbcb1fbec99d65bf59d85c8cb62ee2…

that value is identical for every user with this password, on every
site that made the same mistake, and it is precomputed in rainbow
tables you can download. it is also fast: a GPU tries billions per
second, where Argon2id at 64 MiB is bounded by memory it must find
for each guess in parallel

---- not leaking which usernames exist ----
known user, bad password   false (want false)
unknown user               false (want false)

both paths run one full Argon2id, so the two answers take the same
time and the response cannot be used to enumerate accounts
